{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/660148-the-tenth-choir","id":660148,"title":"The Tenth Choir","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-10T18:12:02-07:00","id":660148,"title":"The Tenth Choir","content":"I'm running a campaign in which the Tenth Choir will be the primary antagonists in the background.<br /> <br /> From the B&amp;S book: &quot;Elisabeta the Plague Nun sometimes tells the story of a fraternity of vampires who believed that since their living, hungry death was a curse of God, they must take revenge on the divine. Between the 17th and 20th centuries, the Choir developed a system of blood magic to consort with angels and devils. They drank the blood of angels. They sought to murder God.&quot; <br /> <br /> This game is in the early 19th century Europe. The Tenth Choir is highly active, using a cover of myriad churches and monasteries to conceal themselves. Some of this is true, some is not. However, I could use help deriving the Covenant's unique discipline (or blood sorcery). They indeed are fueled by captive angels whom they draw their blood from. They're not likely to consort with devils like Belial's Brood (which I wish to keep a separate thing). Any suggestions on what to do as the blood sorcery? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1554-vesper","name":"Vesper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T18:52:12-07:00","id":660210,"title":"","content":"There's surprising little demonology in Belial's Brood, outside of its namesake.<br /> <br /> You might look to the <i>Blood Sorcery: Sacraments &amp; Blasphemies</i> book, which has Awakening-like ritual magic as well as a few odds and ends. Just based on the blurb, though, it looks like you could get away with having it be in a Discipline format, at least mechanically, with five abilities of increasing power, if you wanted to be lazy you could look at Disciplines like Essentiaphagia, which lets you interact with and eventually commit diablerie on ghosts, or Blood Tenebrous which lets you interact with spirits, and alter them to fit angels, even if you don't copy them they're good inspiration for seeing how vampires deal with otherworldly beings. For a more uniquely blood sorcerous aspect you'd probably go with rituals of different levels, similar to the existing ones, with some unique tie to Humanity that forces them up or down and has requirements to access certain 'ranks' of the power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-10-2015, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T04:29:47-07:00","id":666700,"title":"","content":"It would probably help if you decided what the angels actually are, before deciding what powers the Tenth choir gets from drinking their blood.<br /> <br /> Are they the actual servants of the Big Guy, maker of heaven and earth? Then the powers ought to be miraculous in nature.<br /> <br /> The quantum supercomputer energy constructs of the God-Machine? Then the powers should be about exploiting the secret loopholes in reality and perhaps enhancing the vampire in biomechanical ways. <br /> <br /> Denizens of the astral plane who are the embodiments of what people think angels are? Then their powers would probably be focused on illusion, thoughts, and emotions. <br /> <br /> Supernal denizens who embody primal facets of the universe? Perhaps a system limited by the type of angel blood in the vampire's system, a seraphim of forces and death would provide different abilities than a cherubim of prime and matter, etc, etc, and I'm thinking the vampire can only make use of one angel's blood at a time to keep things interesting. <br /> <br /> And that's just the standard suspects, you could get weirder and have the tenth choir capture Quashmallam for alchemical shenanigans, or Nemeses for gaining powers over fate. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T05:11:56-07:00","id":666760,"title":"","content":"Oh man, what is a Nemeses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T02:36:05-07:00","id":668025,"title":"","content":"Something from Changeling, hobgoblins that are fate's hitmen, who just happen to look like winged humans.<br /> <br /> So while they're never actually called angels, the fact that their occupation is basically &quot;angel of death&quot; and they look like the popular image of angels, so they arguably count as one of the gazillion things that can be called angels in nwod. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T13:21:09-07:00","id":668738,"title":"","content":"Man, learn something new every day. Know what book they're in, by chance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T15:37:43-07:00","id":668896,"title":"","content":"Dancers in the Dusk, Chapter Two: Tangled Fates, pg. 62","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T16:13:42-07:00","id":675758,"title":"","content":"Wow, t